/2603"],"assessed":[]},"bacterium_name_as_value":{"rows":30,"wells":["BY19/0107"],"assessed":[]}}},"crosscheck":{"current":true,"series":103,"class_disagreements":0,"max_abs_difference":{"S: pymannkendall":0.0,"Var(S): pymannkendall":0.0,"Z (continuity-corrected): pymannkendall":0.0,"Sen 90% interval (Gilbert 1987 ranks): numpy":1.942890293094024e-15,"scipy theilslopes interval, reproduced from the same slopes":0.0,"S: scipy kendalltau":0,"Var(S): scipy kendalltau":7.275957614183426e-12,"P(increasing): scipy":2.220446049250313e-16,"Sen slope: scipy theilslopes / numpy":0.0,"Kruskal-Wallis p: scipy":3.3306690738754696e-15,"Fisher exact p (depth counts): scipy":2.3037127760972e-15},"run_with":{"python":"3.12.10","numpy":"2.5.5","scipy":"1.18.1","pymannkendall":"1.4.3"}},"headlines":[{"id":"levels","text":"Of the 203 wells sampled in 2021 to 2025, 107 (53%) had a five-year median above 5.65 mg/L, half the drinking-water limit, and 55 (27%) a median above the limit itself, 11.3 mg/L. 89 of the 203 have a single sample in those years, and the wells are not a representative network; counting only the 106 with at least three samples, 67 (63%) and 32 (30%).","numbers":{"wells":203,"over_half":107,"over_mav":55,"single_sample":89,"three_or_more":{"wells":106,"over_half":67,"over_mav":32}},"how":"wells in the area with at least one observation dated 2021-2025; each well's median of those observations (censored values at half the limit); counted where the median is > 5.65 and > 11.3 mg/L as N (strictly greater); single-sample wells: one observation in 2021-2025; the second count keeps wells with three or more","link":"#/map?mode=median"},{"id":"trend10y","text":"Over the ten years 2016 to 2025, 33 of the 54 wells with enough data (61%) were likely or very likely rising, 22 of them (41%) very likely; 14 (26%) were likely or very likely falling.","numbers":{"assessed":54,"increasing":33,"decreasing":14,"very likely increasing":22,"indeterminate":7,"increasing_if_ties_go_later":33},"how":"wells assessed for 2016-2025 under the data rules (method page); LAWA classes from the Mann-Kendall or seasonal Kendall test; 'likely or very likely rising' = confidence of an increase at least 67%; 'very likely' = at least 90%; the tie range from the sensitivity check that breaks equal distances to the later date","link":"#/trends?win=10y"},{"id":"trend20y","text":"Over the twenty years 2006 to 2025, 41 of the 49 wells with enough data (84%) were likely or very likely rising (40 to 41 depending on how one tie between two sampling dates is broken), 36 of them (73%) very likely; 6 (12%) were likely or very likely falling.","numbers":{"assessed":49,"increasing":41,"decreasing":6,"very likely increasing":36,"indeterminate":2,"increasing_if_ties_go_later":40},"how":"wells assessed for 2006-2025 under the data rules (method page); LAWA classes from the Mann-Kendall or seasonal Kendall test; 'likely or very likely rising' = confidence of an increase at least 67%; 'very likely' = at least 90%; the tie range from the sensitivity check that breaks equal distances to the later date","link":"#/trends?win=20y"},{"id":"rate","text":"Among the 49 wells assessed over 2006 to 2025, the typical (median) Sen slope was 0.13 mg/L a year, about 1.3 mg/L a decade; the middle half of wells lay between 0.05 and 0.23 mg/L a year.","numbers":{"median":0.13272727272728163,"q25":0.05090655509065391,"q75":0.23337932296701197,"wells":49},"how":"the Sen slope (mg/L as N a year) of every well assessed for 2006-2025, whatever its class; median and quartiles (linear interpolation)","link":"#/trends?win=20y&sec=slopes"},{"id":"panel","text":"In the 19 wells sampled in every year from 2006 to 2025 (long-term monitoring wells, 11 of them between the Ashburton and the Rakaia and 1 of them 80 m or deeper), the median of the 19 wells went from 6.9 mg/L in 2006 to 9.6 mg/L in 2025; that median rose by 0.15 mg/L a year (Sen slope; very likely increasing).","numbers":{"wells":19,"ashburton_rakaia":11,"deep":1,"first":6.949999999999999,"last":9.625,"slope":0.15208333333333351,"p_increasing":0.9996711728023411},"how":"wells with at least one observation in each year 2006-2025 (the same wells every year, so a changing network cannot make the trend); each well's yearly median, then the median across the wells; Mann-Kendall and Sen slope on those 20 yearly medians, time in whole years","link":"#/trends?win=20y&sec=panel"},{"id":"depth","text":"Fewer deep wells (80 m or more) had a 2021–2025 median above the limit (4 of 33, 12%) than shallower wells (22 of 79 under 30 m; 29 of 91 at 30–80 m). Deep wells were not lower overall: their median was 6.75 mg/L against 4.6 mg/L under 30 m, and 20 of 33 were above half the limit.","numbers":{"shallow":{"wells":79,"over_mav":22,"over_half":36,"median":4.6},"mid":{"wells":91,"over_mav":29,"over_half":51,"median":8.649999999999999},"deep":{"wells":33,"over_mav":4,"over_half":20,"median":6.75},"unknown":{"wells":0,"over_mav":0,"over_half":0,"median":null}},"how":"as the first finding, split by the well's recorded depth (ECan's wells layer); the median is the median of the wells' five-year medians; Fisher's exact test on the counts above the limit is on the method page","link":"#/trends?win=20y&sec=depth"}],"trend_tables":{"10y":{"all":{"group":"all","assessed":54,"not_assessed":886,"very likely decreasing":5,"likely decreasing":9,"indeterminate":7,"likely increasing":11,"very likely increasing":22,"increasing":33,"decreasing":14,"median_slope":0.13647254064384107,"q25_slope":-0.04123348003680453,"q75_slope":0.28491891573186295},"subarea":[{"group":"Rangitata to Hinds","assessed":11,"not_assessed":113,"very likely decreasing":2,"likely decreasing":2,"indeterminate":4,"likely increasing":1,"very likely increasing":2,"increasing":3,"decreasing":4,"median_slope":0.04884884884884993,"q25_slope":-0.0770673258433065,"q75_slope":0.18572442611914536},{"group":"Hinds to Ashburton","assessed":10,"not_assessed":239,"very likely decreasing"